1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,191
He opened his front door... and stepped onto a beach.

2
00:00:04,441 --> 00:00:08,694
Not his street. Not his city. Sand, and waves, and seagulls.

3
00:00:08,944 --> 00:00:13,202
He turned around. His door was standing alone in the sand.

4
00:00:13,352 --> 00:00:17,225
Behind it, his own hallway. His coat. His shoes.

5
00:00:17,575 --> 00:00:21,917
He ran back inside, slammed the door... and opened it again.

6
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:25,242
Snow. The top of a mountain.

7
00:00:25,792 --> 00:00:27,617
That was the first morning.

8
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:35,161
It took him a week to learn the rules.

9
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:38,402
Every morning, his door opened somewhere new.

10
00:00:38,652 --> 00:00:41,161
He could go out and explore all day.

11
00:00:41,511 --> 00:00:44,780
But at nine o'clock at night, the door would close.

12
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:46,988
Wherever it was. Forever.

13
00:00:47,538 --> 00:00:51,960
So he made one rule of his own. Always be back before nine.

14
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:57,870
Day three. A desert. Luckily, he already had sunglasses.

15
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:02,610
Day eight. The roof of a moving train.

16
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:09,881
Day fourteen. A library with shelves taller than the clouds.

17
00:01:11,831 --> 00:01:16,303
Day twenty. A city he had never seen, glowing in the dark.

18
00:01:18,053 --> 00:01:21,427
Some nights, he made it back with one second to spare.

19
00:01:24,677 --> 00:01:29,575
He quit his job. Why go to work, when the whole world comes to your door?

20
00:01:31,725 --> 00:01:34,576
Then, on day thirty, he opened the door...

21
00:01:34,726 --> 00:01:36,217
and saw a bedroom.

22
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:37,857
His bedroom.

23
00:01:38,207 --> 00:01:41,192
His lamp. His clock. Eight fifty-nine.

24
00:01:41,642 --> 00:01:44,416
And in his bed... someone was asleep.

25
00:01:44,966 --> 00:01:46,391
He walked closer.

26
00:01:47,141 --> 00:01:48,322
It was him.

27
00:01:48,972 --> 00:01:52,788
Behind him, the hallway was gone. Only white fog.

28
00:01:53,138 --> 00:01:55,681
And then he remembered the first morning.

29
00:01:55,931 --> 00:01:57,750
His alarm never rang.

30
00:01:58,099 --> 00:01:59,965
Because he never woke up.

31
00:02:00,315 --> 00:02:04,165
The beach. The snow. The train. Thirty days of doors...

32
00:02:04,315 --> 00:02:06,369
all inside one long dream.

33
00:02:06,819 --> 00:02:11,522
And the door that closes at nine... was his last chance to wake up.

34
00:02:11,872 --> 00:02:15,103
He grabbed his own shoulder, and shook it. Hard.

35
00:02:15,653 --> 00:02:17,409
The clock clicked to nine.

36
00:02:19,007 --> 00:02:22,987
He opened his eyes. Morning light. A normal Tuesday.

37
00:02:23,337 --> 00:02:26,383
He was home. He was awake. He was sure of it.

38
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:29,989
He walked to the front door, and reached for the handle.

39
00:02:30,539 --> 00:02:32,528
But before he could open it...

40
00:02:32,878 --> 00:02:35,173
someone on the other side knocked.
